# Implementation Plan: Feature-Based App Router Architecture

Restructure the codebase to enforce a **Feature-Based App Router Architecture directly inside `src/app/`** as mandated by the updated `AGENTS.md`.

---

## Architectural Rules

1. **Feature Code Directly Inside `src/app/<feature>/`**:
   Each feature route directory under `src/app/<feature>/` houses its page implementation (`page.tsx`) along with feature-specific `components/`, `services/`, `types/`, and `index.ts` exports. No separate `src/modules/` directory will be created or maintained.

2. **Global Shared UI & Infrastructure (`src/components/`, `src/data/`)**:
   - `src/components/common/`: Application-wide UI primitives (`Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `SectionHeader`, `DynamicIcon`).
   - `src/components/layout/`: Global layout shells (`Header`, `Footer`, `MobileNav`).
   - `src/components/sections/`: Multi-feature reusable page sections (`HeroSection`, `PlatformStorytelling`, `ProductEcosystem`, `AIAgentShowcase`, `IoTDataFlow`, `WhyEntelgowSection`, `CinematicCTA`).
   - `src/data/`: Global company metadata (`company.ts`).

3. **No `src/modules/` or `src/shared/`**:
   Completely remove `src/modules/` and `src/shared/`.

